Author: Pedro Luiz Ramos [aut, cre],
    Lucas Osses [aut]
Maintainer: Pedro Luiz Ramos <pedro.ramos@uc.cl>
Description: Fits survival trees and random survival forests using
    cure-fraction-oriented splitting for right-censored long-term survival
    data. Node-level long-term survival probabilities are estimated by
    tail-averaged Kaplan-Meier or inverse-probability-of-censoring weighted
    estimators. Honest sample splitting and explicit tail-maturity constraints
    prevent unsupported terminal-node estimates. The forest implementation
    provides out-of-bag prediction, parallel tree construction, split-based
    variable importance, experimental infinitesimal-jackknife diagnostics,
    and coherent estimates of population and susceptible survival.
